WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.333
Since twenty fourteen,
only one in three Croatian primary

00:00:04.383 --> 00:00:08.828
and secondary schools has taken
part in Erasmus+ KA2 partnerships.

00:00:09.228 --> 00:00:10.328
Which schools are they?

00:00:10.728 --> 00:00:11.839
Who do they work with?

00:00:12.239 --> 00:00:13.794
What are their projects about?

00:00:14.194 --> 00:00:16.639
Erasmus+ Kompas answers these questions.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:21.344
KA2 is the Erasmus+
key action in which different

00:00:21.394 --> 00:00:24.506
organisations work together
and share experience.

00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:29.122
Erasmus+ Kompas is designed for schools,

00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:31.747
associations, cities, counties, citizens,

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:35.927
journalists and researchers who want
to learn more about KA2 projects.

00:00:37.077 --> 00:00:39.521
Our data comes from the Erasmus+

00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:42.904
Project Results Platform
and Croatia's Open Data Portal,

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:47.973
which provides datasets from the
Agency for Mobility and EU Programmes

00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:51.134
and registers of educational institutions.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.951
You can explore data by county and topic,

00:00:55.131 --> 00:00:58.464
find projects and organisations,
or ask the Assistant.

00:00:59.614 --> 00:01:02.726
The map shows the share of schools
taking part in each county:

00:01:02.906 --> 00:01:05.794
from fourteen and a half per cent
in Zagreb County

00:01:05.844 --> 00:01:09.178
to almost fifty-seven per cent
in Varaždin County.

00:01:10.328 --> 00:01:12.994
Every organisation has its own page.

00:01:13.394 --> 00:01:16.506
For example,
Gimnazija Metković has taken part

00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:19.667
in twenty-two projects
and coordinated one of them.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.400
The organisation list
can be filtered by county,

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.024
type and period, and downloaded
as a CSV, Excel or PDF file.

00:01:29.174 --> 00:01:32.063
A language model extracted
problems, approaches,

00:01:32.243 --> 00:01:35.132
target groups and results
from the project summaries.

00:01:35.532 --> 00:01:37.977
The concept network
shows related concepts,

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:42.157
such as early school leaving and students
from disadvantaged backgrounds.

00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:47.084
You can also simply ask the Assistant,
in Croatian or English.

00:01:47.484 --> 00:01:49.262
Ask about “dropping out of school”,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.109
and the Assistant
recognises school dropout

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:54.826
by its meaning and finds
five relevant projects,

00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:56.561
with examples and sources.

00:01:57.711 --> 00:02:02.600
The data is processed in Python
and merged into a DuckDB database,

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.891
which is used to build
a static website with Astro.

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:10.069
A language model running
locally processed the summaries,

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:12.916
and an algorithm grouped related concepts.

00:02:13.316 --> 00:02:16.871
When a user asks a question,
the model only routes it.

00:02:17.271 --> 00:02:20.160
Tools retrieve the data,
and code writes the answer.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.893
So the figures come from the data,
not from the model.

00:02:25.043 --> 00:02:28.599
Schools can see which organisations
in their county already

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:31.538
take part in projects and what
those projects are about.

00:02:31.938 --> 00:02:35.049
Citizens, journalists
and researchers can easily

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:37.988
learn more about
KA2 partnerships in their area.

00:02:39.138 --> 00:02:41.360
Planned next steps
are a partner search tool,

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.873
a guide for first projects,

00:02:43.053 --> 00:02:46.164
an annual data refresh and a public API.
